%%label I. Adagio
%%note E minor. A two-bar subject (B, E, F sharp, G held as a suspension) passes from violin to right hand to bass; two circle-of-fifths episodes, a chromatic lament bass, and a return over a tonic pedal.
X:1
T:Bach’s Missing Violin Sonata
T:I. Adagio
C:Lor, in the manner of J. S. Bach
M:4/4
L:1/16
Q:"Adagio" 1/4=38
%%score 1 {2 3}
% Dynamics are balance marks for the site's sampled playback: its violin sample is about 12 dB louder than its piano sample, so the violin is marked several levels below the keyboard. These marks are a playback compromise, not dynamics for live players.
V:1 clef=treble name="Violin"
V:2 clef=treble name="Kbd. r.h."
V:3 clef=bass name="Kbd. l.h."
K:Em
V:1
%%MIDI program 40
V:2
%%MIDI program 0
V:3
%%MIDI program 0
% bars 1-2: subject in the violin over a descending bass (E D C B); counter-melody in the right hand
[V:1] !pp!B2e2 f3g- g4- g2f2 | e2b2- bagf e2^d2 !trill!f3e |
[V:2] !f!GFGB BABd eAce ^d2BF | GBeB ceAc B2F2- F2z2 |
[V:3] !f!E,2G,2 D,2B,,2 C,2A,,2 B,,2A,,2 | G,,2E,2 A,2F,2 B,4 B,,4 |
% bars 3-4: the two upper voices exchange parts; the close turns to G major
[V:1] e2EB BABd eAce ^d2BF | GBeB cAFc B2c2 cfac' |
[V:2] B2e2 f3g- g4- g2f2 | e2b2- bagf g2e2 !trill!a3g |
[V:3] E,2G,2 D,2B,,2 C,2A,,2 B,,2A,,2 | G,,2E,2 A,2D,2 G,2C,2 D,2D,,2 |
% bars 5-6: first episode. A chain of sevenths round the circle of fifths; each voice in turn holds its note as a suspension
[V:1] !ppp!(bd'c'b-) b4 (ac'ba-) a4 | (gd'bg-) g4 (fc'af-) f4 |
[V:2] !mf!g4 egfe- e4 dfed- | d4 cgec- c4 BdgB |
[V:3] !mf!G,,2B,,2 C,2E,2 F,2A,2 B,2D,2 | E,2G,2 A,2C,2 D,2F,2 G,2D,2 |
% bars 7-8: the violin climbs to its first peak and both close in B minor
[V:1] !<(!egb^c' !<)!!pp!d'3c' bagf efge | d3^c !trill!c3B B4 zfed |
[V:2] B2^c2 ^AcAe d2B2 G2B2- | B3^A AFE2 D4 z2B2 |
[V:3] E,2G,2 F,2F,,2 G,,2B,,2 E,2^C,2 | F,4 F,,4 B,,2D,2 B,,2E,,2 |
% bars 9-10: the subject in the bass, in B minor
[V:1] !pp!^c2d2 e3d dfb2- b2gf | d2^c2- cfb^c' d'2c'2 ^a3b |
[V:2] !f!^A2B2 G3F F2GB e2A2 | B2^A2- A2B2 f2e2- e3d |
[V:3] !f!F,,2B,,2 ^C,3D,- D,4- D,2C,2 | B,,2F,2- F,E,D,^C, B,,2^A,,2 !trill!C,3B,, |
% bars 11-12: second episode. The chain of sevenths again, back towards E minor, now with quick turns
[V:1] !ppp!b4 (ga/b/ag-) g4 (fg/a/gf-) | f4 (ef/g/fe-) e4 (^de/f/ed) |
[V:2] !mf!de/f/ed- d4 cd/e/dc- c4 | Bc/d/cB- B4 AB/c/BA- A4 |
[V:3] !mf!B,,2D,2 E,2G,2 A,2C,2 D,2F,2 | G,2B,,2 C,2E,2 F,2A,,2 B,,2B,2 |
% bars 13-15: lament. The bass sinks by semitones from E to B while the violin rises against it
[V:1] !ppp!e4- egfe f4- fagf | !<(!^g4- gbag a4- a^c'ba | a4- a2^a2 !<)!!pp!b4 b=agf |
[V:2] !mf!GBAG- G4 FAGF- F4 | E^GFE- E4 A^cBA- A4 | AcBA e4 e2^d2 f2z2 |
[V:3] !mf!E,2E,2E,2E,2 ^D,2D,2D,2D,2 | D,2D,2D,2D,2 ^C,2C,2C,2C,2 | C,2C,2C,2C,2 B,,2B,,2B,,2B,,2 |
% bars 16-17: return. The subject in the right hand, a descant above it in the violin
[V:1] !pp!egbg bfbd' e'ac'e' ^d'2bf | g2b2 c'2a2 b4 a4 |
[V:2] !f!B2e2 f3g- g4- g2f2 | e2b2- bagf e2^d2 !trill!f3e |
[V:3] !f!E,2G,2 D,2B,,2 C,2A,,2 B,,2A,,2 | G,,2E,2 A,2F,2 B,4 B,,4 |
% bar 18: interrupted cadence, Neapolitan sixth, dominant
[V:1] g2c'2- c'ba2- a2=f2 ^d3e |
[V:2] ecge ecAc AcAc BAFA |
[V:3] C,2E,2 A,2G,2 =F,2A,,2 B,,4 |
% bars 19-20: the subject's head once more over a tonic pedal; major close
[V:1] !ppp!e2Be f3g- g4- g2f2 | !fermata!^g12 z4 |]
[V:2] !mf!GFGB ^dBde cecA AcAd | !fermata![Be]12 z4 |]
[V:3] !mf!E,2E,2E,2E,2 E,2E,2E,2E,2 | !fermata![E,,E,]12 z4 |]
